# Verification comments

- Every check in `verify()` and its verification helpers must have an adjacent
  comment explaining what it checks and why the restriction is needed.
- Apply this to all configuration scripts and shared verification helpers,
  including functions such as `verify_rule()` and `verify_map()`.
- Keep comments concise and specific to the check. A function docstring or error
  message does not replace the comment for an individual check.
- Update the comment when the check's behavior changes.

```python
# Pairing type and code is unambiguous only with one value of each.
if type_count and code_count and (type_count != 1 or code_count != 1):
    raise ValidationError('Specify exactly one ICMP type and code when using both.')
```
